Quartz countertops consist of roughly 90 % natural quartz crystals bound with high performance resins, polymers and pigments; the mixture undergoes high pressure, high temperature processing that yields non porous slabs noted for scratch resistance, stain resistance and low maintenance compared with natural stone.
The sector benefits from expanding residential remodeling activity, heightened consumer preference for hygienic surfaces and increased specification of quartz in hospitality and office fit outs; meanwhile manufacturers are launching ultra compact slabs and digital print veining designs that broaden design flexibility while supporting sustainability goals.
